    - target: {fileID: 7280319124748709216, guid: 9b8f1db92aa53214f9f3590643d0ab96, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "A Rubber Ducky is a USB device that looks like a regular flash drive
        but acts like a keyboard when plugged into a computer. It automatically types
        out pre-programmed keystrokes at high speed, executing commands or scripts
        without needing user input. \n\nOften used by security professionals for
        penetration testing, it can simulate a human typing, making it a powerful
        tool for exploiting systems if physical access is gained. In the wrong hands,
        it can be used to quickly deploy malware or extract sensitive data."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7280319124748709216, guid: 9b8f1db92aa53214f9f3590643d0ab96, type: 3}
